      "label": "Harmful",
      "description": "The meme references a generational memory of using 'eat my ass' as an insult, which may unintentionally echo historical racial stereotypes associated with Black people, such as animalistic caricatures. While the phrase itself is not inherently racial, its use in this context may implicitly reference or rely on these stereotypes, which are part of the broader cultural context of racialized language. This can be perceived as harmful due to its potential to reinforce or normalize offensive historical associations.",
